To: port-alpha@netbsd.org
Date: Sun, 30 Dec 2001 21:55:43 +0000
Subject: Booting from more than one boot partition.....

I finally got around to trying this out a few days ago. 

If I set the bootdef_dev variable in the SRM to multiple devices
with a comma between them then the SRM will attempt to boot from one
until it gets to a device that actually works. I configured my test
box to boot from the CD-ROM and then the hard drive, figuring this
would be handy when the machine is turned into a read-only firewall
later.

Pretty slick.
